# His request, built by the pipeline (PC13, docs/2026-11-08-pipeline-canvas-phasemap.spec) — James, 2026-11-13: "put a pin in the can be moved
# anywhere. need the pipeline building all of my requests." · "like the pipeline can build all of this if we get ollama working with emerge and the pipeline"
# His words → the intent (a gap holds the run and is asked of him) → a phase written from his words (docs/2026-11-13-his-requests-phasemap.spec,
# HR<n>) → Idearium's own build pipeline, run as one step (built on the Ollama ladder first, landed, evidence holding for his yes). Every step is a
# route Idearium already serves. Typed in COS's console: request <his words>.
envelope: 1
uuid: nexus-export-pipeline-his-request
type: pipeline
id: his-request
context: Idearium › pipelines (served at GET /api/pipelines, run by COS)
intent: >-
  His words built by the pipeline: the intent and its gaps (asked of him), a phase written from his words, then Idearium's build pipeline for it.
summary: 4 tasks · Idearium's own routes · the build pipeline as a step
system: idearium
tags:
  - pipeline
  - idearium
  - request
  - bundled
source: idearium/pipelines
occurrences: 1
payload:
  id: his-request
  format: nexus-pipeline
  version: 1
  name: His request
  description: >-
    His words built by the pipeline. The intent (the context needed, the DAG, what is found, the gaps): a gap holds the run with its question,
    his answers go in vars.answers and Continue asks again. Then a phase is written from his words into his requests' map, and Idearium's build
    pipeline builds it (Ollama's ladder first; evidence holds for his yes).
  vars:
    words: ''          # his request, verbatim
    answers: '{}'      # his answers to the gaps, as JSON: { "<gap id>": "<answer>" }
    repo: nexus
    map: docs/2026-11-13-his-requests-phasemap.spec
  settings:
    parallel: 1
  tasks:
    - id: intent
      label: What he means, what it needs, what is missing
      depends_on: []
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/repos/{{vars.repo}}/intent
          method: POST
          body: '{"text":{{vars.words | json}},"answers":{{vars.answers}}}'
          timeoutMs: 120000
      gate:
        matches: '"blockedBy":\[\]'
        reasonAt: body.gaps
      onFail: hold   # a gap: answer it (vars.answers), then Continue
    - id: phase
      label: His request written as a phase
      depends_on:
        - intent
      step:
        type: api
        config:
          url: nexus://idearium/api/repos/{{vars.repo}}/phases/add
          method: POST
          body: '{"map":{{vars.map | json}},"title":{{vars.words | slice:0,90 | json}},"does":{{vars.words | json}},"prefix":"HR"}'
      gate:
        contains: '"id":"HR'
    - id: build
      label: Built by Idearium's build pipeline
      depends_on:
        - phase
      step:
        type: pipeline
        config:
          pipeline: Idearium build pipeline
          vars:
            repo: '{{vars.repo}}'
            phase: '{{tasks.phase.output.body.id}}'
            does: '{{vars.words}}'
            why: 'his request'
    - id: told
      label: Said to him
      depends_on:
        - build
      step:
        type: notify
        config:
          title: Your request was built
          body: '{{tasks.phase.output.body.id}}: {{vars.words | slice:0,120}}'
